<title>ESTONIA: HOIU SEEKS INTERNATIONAL LOAN.</title>
<headline>HOIU SEEKS INTERNATIONAL LOAN.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hoiupank, the third largest bank in Estonia, said on Tuesday it hopes to sign an international loan agreement in two weeks.</p>
<p>&quot;We are holding negotiations with foreign institutions... we hope to conclude a loan in two weeks,&quot; Heino Viik, director of the bank's finance division, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The sum will be similar to Tallinna Pank's syndicated loan,&quot; Viik added.</p>
<p>Tallinna Pank on Monday signed a 50 million DM syndicated loan agreement.  </p>
<p>&quot;The bank is growing fast and the loan is needed to finance this growth,&quot; Viik said.</p>
<p>Hoiupank also wants to repay some former loans with relatively high interest rates, he added.</p>
<p>He provided no further details.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
